2026-10-24T05:51:30.4918068Z Linux USB/IP device management (experimental preview)
2026-10-24T05:51:30.4918352Z 
2026-10-24T05:51:30.4918445Z Usage: rustusb [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>
2026-10-24T05:51:30.4918611Z 
2026-10-24T05:51:30.4918681Z Commands:
2026-10-24T05:51:30.4919021Z   diagnostics         Export bounded private diagnostics without changing or stopping USB devices
2026-10-24T05:51:30.4919549Z   logs                Read sanitized stored logs or authorized agent audit projections
2026-10-24T05:51:30.4920044Z   agent               Run or query the nonroot shared application service using fixed profiles
2026-10-24T05:51:30.4920663Z   secure-server       Serve configured devices with mandatory mutual TLS and per-device authorization
2026-10-24T05:51:30.4921327Z   secure-discover     Read the stable-key device catalog over the configured mutually authenticated TLS endpoint
2026-10-24T05:51:30.4921996Z   secure-attach       Import the configured stable device key and own its encrypted VHCI relay until stopped
2026-10-24T05:51:30.4922627Z   native-pending      Inspect unresolved secure Native channels through the root helper (root only)
2026-10-24T05:51:30.4923257Z   native-reconcile    Verify a stopped Native channel and retire its record (root only; no USB writes)
2026-10-24T05:51:30.4923860Z   physical-pending    Inspect unresolved physical grants through the root helper (root only)
2026-10-24T05:51:30.4924495Z   physical-reconcile  Verify restored physical state and retire its grant record (root only; no USB writes)
2026-10-24T05:51:30.4925185Z   physical-server     Serve explicitly authorized whole USB devices through Linux USBFS (experimental, no TLS)
2026-10-24T05:51:30.4925868Z   virtual-server      Serve two virtual test devices; this experimental mode provides no authentication or TLS
2026-10-24T05:51:30.4926525Z   devices             Scan local devices without changing drivers. Discovery is not compatibility validation
2026-10-24T05:51:30.4927120Z   doctor              Read installed tool, module and helper capabilities without loading modules
2026-10-24T05:51:30.4928002Z   discover            Query a server's USB/IP device list over an administrator-managed trusted network
2026-10-24T05:51:30.4928608Z   export              Export an administrator-allowlisted device fingerprint via the privileged helper
2026-10-24T05:51:30.4929167Z   unexport            Release an allowlisted export and request local driver reattachment
2026-10-24T05:51:30.4929675Z   attach              Import a remote bus ID through an allowlisted endpoint and Linux VHCI
2026-10-24T05:51:30.4930129Z   detach              Disconnect an authorized local VHCI port (0..255)
2026-10-24T05:51:30.4930570Z   sessions            Read authoritative native kernel session state through the helper
2026-10-24T05:51:30.4930975Z   status              Query helper and kernel status
2026-10-24T05:51:30.4931330Z   help                Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
2026-10-24T05:51:30.4931592Z 
2026-10-24T05:51:30.4931659Z Options:
2026-10-24T05:51:30.4931955Z       --json                           Emit machine-readable JSON to stdout; logs remain on stderr
2026-10-24T05:51:30.4932848Z       --socket <SOCKET>                Root-owned local helper socket [default: /run/rustusb/control.sock]
2026-10-24T05:51:30.4933438Z       --timeout <TIMEOUT>              Discovery timeout covering DNS, connect and response [default: 10]
2026-10-24T05:51:30.4933913Z       --log-json                       Emit JSON tracing logs on stderr
2026-10-24T05:51:30.4934672Z       --log-directory <LOG_DIRECTORY>  Write sanitized bounded NDJSON to an existing private directory instead of stderr
